This file contains three types of damaged input:
1. Wrong number of fields: P1002 has only four fields.
2. Non-numeric amount: P1003 has ABC instead of a number.
3. Empty line: There is a blank line between P1004 and P1005.
Improve the validation in PassStore
The earlier find() method checked only the number of fields. That means P1003 could incorrectly be accepted because it contains five fields even though its amount is invalid.

Use this improved validation method:

private boolean isValid(String[] fields) {

    if (fields.length != 5) {
        return false;
    }

    try {
        Integer.parseInt(fields[3]);
        double amount = Double.parseDouble(fields[4]);

        if (fields[0].isEmpty() ||
            fields[1].isEmpty() ||
            fields[2].isEmpty() ||
            amount < 0 ||
            !Double.isFinite(amount)) {
            return false;
        }

        return true;

    } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
        return false;
    }
}



